<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's consumer credit raises profits.</title>
<headline>Morocco's consumer credit raises profits.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's consumer credit firm DIAC MAROC said on Wednesday its net profits rose to 23.6 million dirhams ($2.56 million) in 1996 from 15.5 million dirhams in 1995.</p>
<p>Turnover for 1996 was 120.6 million dirhams, the firm said but gave no comparative figures for 1995.</p>
<p>One of the 47 stocks listed on the Casablanca stock exchange, it was last traded at 576 dirhams.</p>
<p>($ = 9.2 dirhams)</p>
<p>- Rabat newsroom +212-772 65 18</p>
</text>
